"""Reviewed Space Center, Seashore House, and Gabby/Ty terminal speech."""
ROWS = []
def add(key, labels, subject, lines):
    replies = [s.strip() for s in lines.split('|')]
    assert len(replies) == 11, (key, len(replies))
    ROWS.append(dict(key='hoenn_battle_endpoint_' + key, labels=labels.split(), subject=subject, replies=replies))

add('space_unannounced','MossdeepCity_SpaceCenter_1F_Text_Grunt1PostBattle','A grunt concludes future invasions should be unannounced.',
'''annoyed~The problem was the stealing, not the quality of the invitation.|He has revised the announcement instead of examining the objective.|Wrong lesson. Leave the center alone.|It's unsettling hearing someone make the harmful part sound settled.|The staff deserve more than a less polite version of the same trouble.|An antagonist has mistaken a presentation note for a moral revision.|A spectacularly narrow interpretation of what went wrong.|The method and purpose need review beyond how early anyone was warned.|A hidden harm doesn't become kinder by arriving quietly.|Changing the entrance won't improve the conduct wearing it.|I'd notice what he still refuses to question while planning the next approach.''')
add('space_post','MossdeepCity_SpaceCenter_1F_Text_Grunt2PostBattle','On a later talk the defeated guard asks us to report he never abandoned his post.',
'''neutral~His next worry is the boss's review, not why the post needed defending.|He is focused on compliance rather than the consequences of the assignment.|Tell the truth. He still chose what he was guarding.|He sounds more worried about blame than angry with us.|Fear of punishment doesn't make this a good place to work.|A defeated guard has requested a favorable narrator for his performance report.|An unfortunate career built around how convincingly one remains in the way.|He could ask what the duty served instead of only whether he fulfilled it.|A command can make a very small room around a person's choices.|He wants his loyalty seen. I hope he also learns to question where it goes.|I'd remember both the fear in his request and the choice he still made.''')
add('space_roll','MossdeepCity_SpaceCenter_1F_Text_Grunt3PostBattle','A defeated grunt warns one win does not establish a winning streak.',
'''smug~One win is indeed one win. We have not rented a parade.|He's right that the next opponent still needs independent attention.|We'll stay ready. No need to argue the count.|He sounds as if he wants the result to feel smaller.|The team still deserves a quick check after the match.|A defeated obstacle has supplied a useful warning in an ungracious wrapper.|A rather sharp way to state extremely basic arithmetic.|We can carry the information forward without borrowing his mood.|A step won doesn't remove the need for the next careful step.|The warning can be useful without making the delivery appealing.|I'd watch what changes ahead rather than stand here discussing our reputation.''')
add('space_fuel','MossdeepCity_SpaceCenter_1F_Text_Grunt4PostBattle','A grunt does not know the fuel\'s purpose and sends us to the leader upstairs.',
'''neutral~He has helped steal something without reading the important part.|The admission reveals a lack of understanding, not a harmless objective.|Ask before helping, not only after getting caught.|It's unsettling when the people doing the work don't know what it's for.|The staff's work shouldn't become an ingredient in somebody else's blind plan.|The supporting cast has not been given the central motivation.|A remarkably important omission in the job briefing.|The fuel's role and risks need actual explanation.|A hand can carry something dangerous without knowing the weight of the choice.|A uniform shouldn't replace having a reason for what you do.|I'd remember how casually he passed the responsibility upstairs.''')
add('space_useful','MossdeepCity_SpaceCenter_2F_Text_Grunt5PostBattle','After the three-battle sequence a grunt wonders whether they help the leader at all.',
'''neutral~A better question might be whether the leader is asking anything worthwhile.|Usefulness to a supervisor isn't the same as a good result for everyone affected.|Question the goal too. Not just the performance.|He sounds ready to doubt something, which could be a beginning.|The people working here deserve to count in that question.|A supporting character has noticed the possibility of an unhelpful role.|The performance review is missing the much larger problem with the production.|He should assess purpose and consequences alongside efficiency.|A person can choose more than becoming a better instrument for someone else.|Loyalty isn't much of a fit if it leaves no room to think.|I'd hope his next question reaches beyond how pleased the boss might be.''')
add('space_three_mess','MossdeepCity_SpaceCenter_2F_Text_Grunt6PostBattle','Afterward a grunt laments that three members still lost.',
'''smug~A larger committee has produced the same awkward conclusion.|Numerical advantage doesn't ensure sound individual decisions or coordination.|Three people still need a working plan.|It must feel embarrassing after sounding so certain before the matches.|More opponents shouldn't mean less care for anyone's Pokemon.|An imposing ensemble has discovered that size is not the entire script.|A regrettable loss with an unusually crowded debriefing.|Review the actual choices instead of treating headcount as a guarantee.|Many feet can still follow one unhelpful direction.|A united appearance doesn't automatically create a useful combination.|I'd notice whether they learn anything beyond how bad the result looks.''')
add('space_triple','MossdeepCity_SpaceCenter_2F_Text_Grunt7PostBattle','A grunt says their three losses look three times worse.',
'''smug~He has added multiplication to the disappointment department.|The scale of embarrassment doesn't explain what failed in each match.|Looks don't fix it. Review the decisions.|It's hard when everyone around you shares the same rough moment.|A rest would help more than counting how many times the team felt bad.|A disappointing scene has received an unnecessarily elaborate numerical review.|Their misery has acquired a small but dedicated accounting office.|Separate the three attempts so each can offer useful feedback.|A hard moment needn't grow heavier because others saw it too.|An unflattering result isn't improved by making it the whole group identity.|I'd rather hear what one of them would change than another way to count the shame.''')
add('dwayne','Route109_SeashoreHouse_Text_DwaynePostBattle','Dwayne enjoys fierce Slateport battles followed by cold Soda Pop.',
'''soft_smile~A very warm afternoon with a deliberately cold closing act.|He has found an enjoyable routine around the challenge and recovery.|Good plan. Let the Pokemon settle too.|It's nice having a little ordinary reward after the excitement.|A cold drink and a proper pause make a pleasant finish.|A satisfying outing can contain both action and an unhurried epilogue.|A dramatic temperature contrast I can understand without additional lore.|Recovery should fit the activity instead of merely decorating it.|A familiar little pleasure can make effort feel more welcoming.|He knows what makes the whole day enjoyable, not just the score.|I'd remember how his expression changes once the battle is behind him.''')
add('johanna','Route109_SeashoreHouse_Text_JohannaPostBattle','Johanna is thirsty and considers a Soda Pop.',
'''soft_smile~Her next opponent is a rather ordinary thirst.|Taking care of a basic need is a sensible next step after exertion.|Get a drink and rest. The match can wait.|She sounds relieved to have the difficult part finished.|A quiet seat and something to drink seem well earned.|The battle scene has yielded to a much more manageable little problem.|A refreshingly practical ending to a competitive afternoon.|A pause gives her time to notice what she needs.|An ordinary comfort can make room after a busy moment.|Nobody needs to make recovering look impressive.|I'd let her enjoy the break instead of turning it into another conversation she must carry.''')
add('simon','Route109_SeashoreHouse_Text_SimonPostBattle','Simon imagines replacing his inner tube with a Pokemon that can carry him on water.',
'''soft_smile~A flotation device with friendship and its own lunch requirements.|A capable partner can open routes, but its needs remain part of the plan.|Keep the tube until he's actually prepared.|It must sound lovely to travel with someone you trust.|The Pokemon deserves care beyond being a more convenient seat.|The prop may change, but the new companion should never become only a prop.|A practical ambition with a much more demanding care schedule.|He should learn the travel requirements before discarding useful equipment.|Being carried by a life asks for more attention than being held by air.|Convenience is appealing when the partner's comfort stays visible.|I'd like to see how they learn to move comfortably together.''')
add('gabby_shortteam','GabbyAndTy_Text_GabbyNotEnoughMons','Gabby searches for a strong trainer with more Pokemon instead of accepting our current team.',
'''soft_smile~The interview has a very particular casting brief.|Their double-battle format needs two eligible partners.|We'll return ready. No need to audition unprepared.|It's awkward being looked past when you don't fit the plan.|A second partner should be ready, not added only for the camera.|The reporter is seeking a scene before meeting the person inside it.|A talent search has collided with a fairly basic headcount.|We can choose a coordinated pair before trying their format.|A small group can still have worth beyond what a producer wants.|An incomplete fit for the footage isn't a flaw in the team.|I'd rather meet their interest on fair terms than rush to look impressive.''')
add('ty_shortteam','GabbyAndTy_Text_TyNotEnoughMons','Ty says a larger team would improve his footage.',
'''soft_smile~Our team has received a note from the camera department.|A richer image isn't the only consideration in preparing a fair battle.|Team comes before footage. Bring two when we're ready.|I'd feel uncomfortable being measured by how much there is to film.|The Pokemon shouldn't be rushed into a match to improve a shot.|The cameraman has offered an extremely practical, if narrow, casting criticism.|A reminder that the lens is not an impartial judge of what matters.|The format needs a pair; the picture is a separate preference.|A life can be fully present without filling the frame.|Good composition should work with the people and Pokemon actually there.|I'd rather notice one comfortable partner than fill the view with ones who aren't ready.''')
add('ty_footage','GabbyAndTy_Text_TyPostBattle','Ty praises us as a natural subject and celebrates the footage.',
'''soft_smile~We have apparently battled our way into a very favorable camera review.|A spontaneous performance can look natural after a great deal of unseen practice.|Glad he got something useful. Check everyone's comfortable with it.|It's flattering, though I don't think I'd know where to put my hands now.|The team's care matters after the interesting part has been filmed.|The unwitting protagonist has acquired an enthusiastic cinematographer.|A rare occasion when being watched has produced a complimentary result.|I'd be curious which moment showed what the battle actually felt like.|A recorded little moment can hold more than its subject intended.|Natural doesn't mean effortless; it means the work stopped looking forced.|I'd like to see what he noticed that we were too busy battling to catch.''')
add('gabby_decline','GabbyAndTy_Text_DontGiveUpKeepingEyeOut','Gabby accepts a declined or canceled interview and says they will watch for us.',
'''soft_smile~No interview today. Our entire career has not therefore ended.|Declining publicity isn't the same as abandoning training.|We can pass on the camera and keep going.|It's nice the invitation survives, even if the encouragement guesses too much.|A quiet choice is allowed to be a good one.|A character can decline the narration without leaving the adventure.|A refusal with a surprisingly ambitious motivational footnote.|We can return if we actually want to share a quote later.|A story needn't be broadcast to remain worth living.|Being interested in us doesn't make every moment available for display.|I'd keep the friendliness while letting the no remain a complete answer.''')
add('gabby_revisit','GabbyAndTy_Text_KeepingAnEyeOutForYou','Gabby says the reporters will watch for us on future travels.',
'''soft_smile~The road has acquired a small, enthusiastic audience.|A later meeting could show changes one encounter cannot capture.|Fine by us. We'll keep choosing our own route.|It's nice being remembered without needing another performance right now.|A familiar greeting can make a long road feel welcoming.|A recurring observer has left the next scene open.|A standing invitation to be noticed, preferably on a day I feel prepared.|We can compare what has changed if the next meeting happens.|A brief connection can stretch gently between two journeys.|Attention feels better when there is room to step out of the spotlight.|I'd enjoy hearing what they remember when we meet without the first surprise.''')
add('gabby_quote','GabbyAndTy_Text_PerfectWellBeSeeingYou','Gabby loves our completed quote and hopes the resulting show airs.',
'''soft_smile~Our small sentence may be about to have a much busier day than we do.|Editing will shape the impression, so the final program may reveal a different perspective.|Hope they use it fairly. The team did the work.|It's strange thinking something you said quickly might be heard far away.|I hope the ordinary care comes through alongside the exciting match.|A closing line has been entrusted to someone else's version of the scene.|My spontaneous wording now has an alarming potential audience.|I'd like to compare the full context with the selected clip.|A small spoken thing can travel farther than its speaker.|A good finish should represent the person, not only flatter the program.|I'd love to see which little moment they choose around the words.''')
